      "name": "Public Measure AM",
      "jurisdiction": "Appanoose County (unincorporated areas)",
      "ballotLanguage": "Shall the following Public Measure be adopted? Question: Shall Appanoose County, Iowa, repeal its existing seven percent (7%) local hotel and motel tax, said repeal being effective December 31, 2026, and impose a replacement seven percent (7%) local hotel and motel tax, beginning January 1, 2027, on the sales price from the renting of lodging in the unincorporated areas of Appanoose County, as authorized by Iowa Code chapter 423A, with the revenues expended in accordance with Iowa Code section 423A.7?"
    }
